# Copy to .env and fill in real values. These placeholders are fake and for
# local development only - never commit real credentials.
#
# The two URLs name DIFFERENT roles, and that separation is what makes row-level
# security real - see "Row-level security" in README.md.
#
# DATABASE_URL is what the app connects through (may point at a pooler, e.g. PgBouncer).
#   Use the application role: not the owner, not a superuser, NOBYPASSRLS. It is
#   subject to every tenant_isolation policy, so it reads nothing until the
#   request declares its organisation.
# DIRECT_URL is used by Prisma Migrate and must point straight at Postgres.
#   Use the owner. It runs DDL, and it is filtered by the same policies for DML.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://openrunic_app:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/openrunic"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://OWNER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/openrunic"
